      <h2 id="virt-removing-wasp-agent_virt-configuring-higher-vm-workload-density" class="group scroll-mt-20">Removing the wasp-agent component<a href="#virt-removing-wasp-agent_virt-configuring-higher-vm-workload-density" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">If you no longer need memory overcommitment, you can remove the <code>wasp-agent</code> component and associated resources from your cluster.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>You have logged in to the cluster with the <code>cluster-admin</code> role.</li>
      <li>You have installed the OpenShift CLI (<code>oc</code>).</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Revert the memory overcommitment configuration by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc patch -n openshift-cnv hyperconvergeds.v1beta1.hco.kubevirt.io kubevirt-hyperconverged \\\n  --type='json' \\\n  -p='[{\"op\": \"remove\", \"path\": \"/spec/higherWorkloadDensity\"}]'"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Delete the <code>MachineConfig</code> that provisions swap memory by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete machineconfig 90-worker-swap"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Verification</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
